course: dictionary
lesson: 12686
title: One word, two meanings: diva
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A diva is a famous, very talented female singer, especially in opera. In a music lesson, you might read: «The opera diva sang high notes that filled the whole theatre.» The clues are opera, high notes and theatre, so the word means a singer.
explain: In everyday talk, diva has a second meaning that is informal and disapproving. «He is a bit of a diva: he wants a special chair, a red carpet and his own room.» The clues are special chair, red carpet and his own room, so here a diva is someone who expects special treatment and makes a fuss.
explain: Always check which meaning fits. Swap your meaning into the sentence. Singing words point to the first meaning. Demands and fuss point to the second.
fact: A diva is a famous, very talented female singer, especially in opera.
fact: In informal talk, a diva is someone who acts as if they are very important and expects special treatment.
fact: «Diva behaviour» means demanding and fussy behaviour.
fact: Useful phrases include «opera diva», «pop diva» and «a bit of a diva».
fact: The plural of diva is divas.
exercise: «The opera diva sang high notes that filled the whole theatre.» What is a diva in this sentence? | A small, quiet instrument | A fussy person who wants special treatment | *A famous, very talented female singer | A kind of theatre seat
exercise: «He is a bit of a diva: he wants a special chair, a red carpet and his own room.» What does diva mean here? | *Someone who expects special treatment and makes a fuss | A large room | A famous singer on a stage | A kind of red carpet
exercise: «Her diva behaviour made the rehearsal take twice as long.» What does diva behaviour mean? | Calm and quiet waiting | *Demanding and fussy behaviour | Singing very loudly | Learning new songs
test: «The pop diva signed autographs for her fans after the show.» What does diva mean in this sentence? | A type of show | A fussy person who wants special treatment | A fan club | *A famous singer
test: Which sentence uses diva in the fussy, informal sense? | «The diva sang the high notes in the opera.» | «The diva's voice was loud and clear.» | «A diva is a famous singer who performs in Italy.» | *«Stop being such a diva and just sit down.»
exam: Read «Her diva behaviour made the rehearsal take twice as long.» What does it tell you about her? | She was happy to wait her turn | She sang very quietly | She was late because of the rain | *She wanted special treatment and made a fuss
